@node Standard Feature Identifiers
@appendix Standard Feature Identifiers
An implementation may provide any or all of the feature identifiers
listed below for use by @nc{cond-expand} and features, but must not
provide a feature identifier if it does not provide the corresponding
feature.

@table @asis
@item @t{r7rs}
All @value{R7RSinitial} Scheme implementations have this feature.

@item @t{exact-closed}
The algebraic operations @code{+}, @code{-}, @code{*}, and @nc{expt}
where the second argument is a non-negative integer produce exact values
given exact inputs.

@item @t{exact-complex}
Exact complex numbers are provided.

@item @t{ieee-float}
Inexact numbers are @acronym{IEEE} 754 binary floating point values.

@item @t{full-unicode}
All Unicode characters present in Unicode version 6.0 are supported as
Scheme characters.

@item @t{ratios}
@code{/} with exact arguments produces an exact result when the divisor
is nonzero.

@item @t{posix}
This implementation is running on a @acronym{POSIX,Portable Operating
System Interface} system.

@item @t{windows}
This implementation is running on Windows.

@item @t{unix, darwin, gnu-linux, bsd, freebsd, solaris, @value{defdots}}
Operating system flags (perhaps more than one).

@item @t{i386}, @t{x86-64}, @t{ppc}, @t{sparc}, @t{jvm}, @t{clr}, @t{llvm}, @value{defdots}
CPU architecture flags.

@item @t{ilp32}, @t{lp64}, @t{ilp64}, @value{defdots}
C memory model flags.

@item @t{big-endian, little-endian}
Byte order flags.

@item @angle{name}
The name of this implementation.

@item @angle{name-version}
The name and version of this implementation.
@end table
